    "body": "Tune the Triton fused MoE kernel configuration for NVIDIA B300 for `E=128, N=768` with BF16. The tuned configuration improves the measured fused MoE kernel latency by **14.21%** over the default heuristic on B300.\r\n\r\n## Motivation\r\n\r\nThe default Triton fused MoE configuration is selected by a heuristic. For the B300 target and the `E=128, N=768` workload, a dedicated tuned configuration provides lower kernel latency.\r\n\r\nThis workload is used by Qwen3-30B-A3B (TP1) and Qwen3-235B-A22B (TP2).\r\n\r\n## Modifications\r\n\r\n- Add a Triton 3.7.1 MoE kernel configuration for:\r\n  - Device: NVIDIA B300 SXM6 PC\r\n  - `E=128`\r\n  - `N=768`\r\n  - BF16\r\n- The configuration was tuned directly on the B300 lane.\r\n- The existing down-projection fallback reuses the up-projection configuration, so no separate `_down` configuration is added.\r\n- No kernel or runtime code changes.\r\n\r\n## Accuracy Tests\r\n\r\nVerified the candidate configuration against the existing `torch_naive_moe` reference across the standard M grid:\r\n\r\n`M = {1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 24, 32, 48, 64, 96, 128, 256, 512, 1024, 1536, 2048, 3072, 4096}`\r\n\r\nConfiguration lookup was also verified to select the new B300 configuration in the candidate arm and fall back to the default heuristic in the baseline arm.\r\n\r\n`test/registered/moe/test_fused_moe.py` passes with the existing BF16 accuracy tolerances.\r\n\r\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\r\n\r\nMeasured `fused_moe_grid_us`, defined as the sum of the per-M median kernel latency across the standard M grid, using CUDA events on NVIDIA B300 SXM6 PC x1.\r\n\r\n8 trials per arm after 2 warmup trials, interleaved ABBA. Lower is better.\r\n\r\n| Arm | n | Median |\r\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\r\n| Baseline | 8 | 1301.70 us |\r\n| Candidate | 8 | 1116.77 us |\r\n\r\nThis corresponds to a **14.21% reduction** in measured fused MoE kernel latency (`0.8579x` baseline).\r\n\r\nThe benchmark was performed on:\r\n\r\n`E=128, N=768, topk=8, hidden=2048, BF16`\r\n\r\nThe search used a pruned configuration space covering block sizes, group size, warp count, and pipeline stages. The final configuration was selected from measurements performed directly on the B300 lane.\r\n\r\nThis is a kernel-level benchmark; no end-to-end model throughput claim is made.\r\n\r\n## Checklist\r\n\r\n- [ ] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\r\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\r\n- [ ] Update documentation according to the [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\r\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to the [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\r\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\r\n\r\n## Review and Merge Process\r\n\r\n1. Ping Merge Oncalls to start the process.\r\n2. Get approvals from CODEOWNERS and other reviewers.\r\n3. Trigger CI tests as required.\r\n4. After green CI and required approvals, ask Merge Oncalls or people with Write permission to merge the PR.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #35990395270](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35990395270)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #35990394932](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35990394932)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #35990395016](https:/